WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back!
-You just said,

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.471
"Jim, I like you
more than I like John Mulaney."

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
I whispered that to you.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:06.673 line:92%
-And I thought that was special.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was a nice thing
to tell you.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was
a nice adjustment there.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do want to ask this
right off the bat.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked last time
you were here about --

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
your wonderful wife, Jeannie,
had a brain tumor.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:20.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-She's doing better.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.554 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-She is doing great.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
once they remove a tumor

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
the size of a pear
from your head,

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're not, you know,
back to 100%,

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
but she's great.
She's --

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
she's taking kids to school.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's writing a book about it.
She's doing great.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously,
you told jokes about it.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-How has that been?

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has that been
a cathartic experience,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
being able
to process it that way?

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's amazing.
You know, yeah.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, my wife and I,
we write everything together.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:49.616 size:88% position:44%
And to do those jokes,
I was kind of surprised,

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, initially,
I was like,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
"All right,
I'm talking about my wife

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
going through
this medical emergency."

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what I realized is that,
as I toured,

00:00:57.323 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
everyone spent those
two-odd weeks in a hospital.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't want
to live in that memory,

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we identify
with that memory.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:07.300 size:84% position:42%
So, yeah, it was great.
It was very cathartic.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.568 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-This is very exciting.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because outside of stand-up,
you also are an actor --

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:15.241
a wonderful one, by my count --
and you have three films

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are gonna be
premiering at Sundance.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am like the Parker Posey...
-Wow!

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:21.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...of Sundance.
-You're the new Parker Posey.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What is unique
about these films --

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.585
It's like,
I normally don't look like this.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:29.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
I gained 80 pounds...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.256 line:92%
...for each of those films.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.493 size:84% position:42%
-So, it just worked out
that all three roles

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.662 line:92%
asked you to gain 80 pounds.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.397 line:92%
-It's an amazing coincidence.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.465 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.467 line:92%
It's an amazing coincidence.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, in the script,
they're like,

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:45.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Very overweight,
super-hot guy."

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:46.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:50.143
And it worked out.
No, but it is so exciting to --

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.213
You know,
'cause I've been acting in stuff

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for 25, 30 years.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:56.382 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And so to have --

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, Sundance is
the be-all, you know, thing.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
So to go there
with three films is amazing,

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
and these are great films,
so I'm excited.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you got to work
with some really great actors.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.861 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, it's amazing.
Like Olivia Colman,

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:11.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
Walton Goggins, Viola Davis,
Allison Janney.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's amazing.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:15.001
-And they were all asked to stay
at their current weights?

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-They were all --

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like --
They were all asked to stay --

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:22.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were like, "Look,
you guys focus on the lines.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.144 line:92%
Jim can do multiple things."

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's --
I mean, I could list --

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.481 line:92%
There's so many amazing actors.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:32.552
Marin Ireland,
who is in an off-Broadway show.

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.586 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I do a film with her.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's an amazing --
I could list every actor,

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:36.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I probably should,
but I won't.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.926
-Well, congratulations on that.
That's very exciting.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:40.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've talked --
[ Applause ]

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, give it up!
-Thank you.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can gain this weight, too!
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can gain this weight
if you try.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.904 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.505 line:92%
If you have a commitment.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.574
-You talked about this, as well.
And I'm very --

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
I look forward to my kids
being old enough

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.410 line:92%
for this to be an option,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you have been touring
internationally.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:00.480
-Yes.
-And using it as an opportunity

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.349
to bring all five of your
children with you on vacations.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.518
-Yes.
Well, you know, jet lag is fun,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:09.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
but jet lag with a 6-year-old
with jet lag is better.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-No, I --

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love, you know,
touring, doing stand-up.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.262
You know,
we've done many shows together.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:19.566
And so, like,
doing these international shows,

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.968
they're an amazing opportunity.
And also, it's --

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, so at Thanksgiving,
I was in Athens.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
I brought my kids
to the Parthenon.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm not Greek.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know I look Greek,
but I'm not.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:30.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so we tooled around Athens
a little bit,

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I did a show,
and it's amazing.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:36.849
-And you took a Greek dance
class with your children?

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.986
-We took a Greek dance --
I thought it was gonna be, like,

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a restaurant,
and my kids were gonna dance,

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was gonna eat a gyro,
you know?

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.058 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:48.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we showed up, and it was,
like, in a dance studio,

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.397 size:78% position:39%
and we did, you know,
some of these dances.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they said,
"All right, now let's get in

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
the traditional Greek outfits,
and I was like, "Okay."

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so --
-And it's fantastic.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yes.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.780 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I will say...

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even if you
took this photo in color,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like it would come out
in black-and-white.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:12.385 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:16.856
-It was so amazing, because I
know I look like a great dancer,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm not.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.059 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I was resistant,

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.629
but it was an amazing experience
to do with your kids.

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:25.832
-And are your children at the
age now where they're laughing

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.300 line:92%
at you being a bad dancer?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.370 size:81% position:41%
-Oh, they laugh at me
just about everything.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there is something
about seeing me dance that bad

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:36.409
where they're like, "Oh,
you're really not good at this."

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.012 size:81% position:41%
You know what I mean?
Are you a good dancer?

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:39.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-'Cause, you know, like,

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:42.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the acting and improv
and stuff like that,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's moments
where you'll see someone --

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.786 size:88% position:44%
You're like, "Oh, wow.
You can't dance at all."

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:49.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm one of those people
that can't.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:49.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:52.191
-You also went to South Africa.
-Went to South Africa.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How was that?
-Amazing.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.029 line:92%
You know, we went on a safari,

00:04:56.029 --> 00:05:00.166
which is essentially just a
fancy word for animal stalking.

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:01.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's all you do.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.038 size:84% position:42%
You just kind of, like,
follow around animals.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:08.107
And it's a good thing they can't
turn you in to the police.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.410
Because they would be like,
"That bald guy over there

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.645
was following me for two hours."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:15.682
"And then, when I woke up,
he was taking pictures of me

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:17.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my family,
and we were naked."

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You know? It's --

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:23.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a very strange thing.
But it is -- it's fascinating.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.090 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's hard to articulate,

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you sit there,
and it is the circle of life.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.495
So, like, you'll sometimes see
an animal kill another animal,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.998
and intellectually, you think,
"Oh, I don't want to see that,"

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:35.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when you're in the moment,
you're like, "Get 'em."

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.002 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:38.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even my 9-year-old daughter,
who loves animals,

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
draws pictures of kittens
all of the time,

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:43.109
She's like, "Get 'em, get 'em!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:45.078 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was funny.

